# Who must review what (GitHub: Settings -> Branches -> "Require review from Code Owners" must be on for this to
# bind). Every file outside parts/ and index/ is a maintainer's: the workflows and these settings (.github/), the store's
# own files (store.json, withdrawn.json, withdrawn/, disputes.json, ecadlib-version.txt) and every top-level file
# (README, CONTRIBUTING, NOTICE, LICENSE). A pull_request check runs the pull request's own copy of the workflows, so
# a change to .github/ is never proven by its own green check: only a maintainer's review stands behind it.
# `ecadlib store-repo init --maintainer NAME` writes the maintainers' GitHub names here; replace the placeholder
# otherwise.
* @MAINTAINERS

# Parts and the index: no code owner. The verify check holds them to the contributor rules (CONTRIBUTING.md), and a
# maintainer still merges.
/parts/
/index/
